5. **Unique Identifying Traits**: The cabbage's unique trait lies in its structure – the tightly packed, layered leaves forming a dense, rounded head. This characteristic sets it apart from other vegetables like lettuce, which have more loosely arranged leaves. Additionally, the presence of the stem adds another distinguishing feature.
